# Site Copy Guard

- For all user-facing copy, write as if the final customer is reading it.
- Do not mention internal work, tests, experiments, iterations, prototypes, drafts, UX strategy, or site optimization decisions in visible text.
- Avoid meta phrases about the website itself unless the user explicitly asks for them.
- Prefer customer-facing wording about service, property, booking, trust, comfort, location, or process.

## Avoid

- "le site est maintenant pensé..."
- "nous testons..."
- "version bêta"
- "expérimentation"
- "prototype"
- "message lisible", "visuels premium", "parcours de conversion" when used as internal design commentary

## Prefer

- Practical benefits for the visitor
- Clear booking or contact steps
- Property and location value
- Professional reassurance without talking about internal design choices
